Marineris branding — licence and additional terms
=================================================

The files in this directory (logo, wordmark, icons, background image and
theme) are part of Marineris and are licensed, like the rest of the project,
under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 (see ../LICENSE),
supplemented by the following additional terms, as permitted by section 7 of
that licence.

1. Origin of the material — section 7(c)

   a. You must not misrepresent the origin of this material. In particular,
      a modified version of Marineris must not be presented as Marineris, as
      an official edition of it, or as endorsed by its authors.

   b. Modified versions of this material must be marked in reasonable ways as
      different from the original version. When you convey a modified version
      of Marineris, or make one available to users interacting with it
      remotely through a network, the reasonable way to do so is to replace
      the logo, wordmark and icons of this directory with your own and to use
      a name other than "Marineris" for your version. Stating that your
      version is based on, or a fork of, Marineris is not a misrepresentation
      and is welcome.

2. Trademarks — section 7(e)

   This licence does not grant any right under trademark law to use the name
   "Marineris" or its logos as the name or logo of a product or service,
   except to identify unmodified copies of Marineris and to refer to the
   project truthfully (for example "based on Marineris").

These additional terms apply only to the files of this directory. They do not
restrict running Marineris, modified or not, on your own servers, studying
it, or sending changes back to the project.
